WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.225
The architecture.

2
00:00:01.225 --> 00:00:07.878
Several Trust Protection Foundation servers
sharing one SQL database form a cluster,

3
00:00:07.878 --> 00:00:12.775
and a message bus, an MQTT broker
using TLS on port 8883, links them.

4
00:00:12.775 --> 00:00:17.387
Each server runs the components you switch
on for it in the Configuration Console.

5
00:00:17.387 --> 00:00:22.574
The ones this guide uses are CA Import,
Certificate Lifecycle and Monitoring,

6
00:00:22.574 --> 00:00:27.437
Certificate Revocation Monitoring,
Network Discovery, the EST service,

7
00:00:27.437 --> 00:00:31.975
Network Device Enrollment for SCEP,
the ACME service and Reporting.

8
00:00:31.975 --> 00:00:37.273
You can keep work on particular servers
with processing engines, discovery zones,

9
00:00:37.273 --> 00:00:40.623
or by turning components
off, and that matters later,

10
00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:43.350
when we keep ACME off
the FIPS-mode servers.

11
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.788
Sizing comes from CyberArk's tables.

12
00:00:45.788 --> 00:00:49.476
Two servers handle up to fifty
thousand active certificates.

13
00:00:49.476 --> 00:00:54.430
Up to two hundred fifty thousand takes
six: two for log and event processing,

14
00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:57.387
two for web services and
two back-end servers.

15
00:00:57.387 --> 00:01:02.388
Past a million, CyberArk designs it with
you, and SQL Enterprise is required.

16
00:01:02.388 --> 00:01:04.338
Each server needs four cores,

17
00:01:04.338 --> 00:01:08.076
sixteen gigabytes of memory
and five gigabytes of disk.

18
00:01:08.076 --> 00:01:12.662
For availability: Always On for the
database, at least two servers per role,

19
00:01:12.662 --> 00:01:17.625
and a load balancer in front of the web
services, which rolling upgrades require.

20
00:01:17.625 --> 00:01:22.831
For the CAs, a Microsoft CA Pool holds
up to three CA templates; if the first

21
00:01:22.831 --> 00:01:28.037
CA fails, the platform stops querying
it for sixty minutes and fails over.

22
00:01:28.037 --> 00:01:33.500
Sources: CyberArk 26.1 System
Requirements (cluster, Message Bus,

23
00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:39.066
sizing, ports, network scoping);
Installation and Upgrade Guide pp.

24
00:01:39.066 --> 00:01:42.571
54 and 86–94 (components);
Rolling upgrades;

25
00:01:42.571 --> 00:01:48.600
Always On high availability; Create
and configure a Microsoft CA Pool.
